Experience points themselves are useless. The only worthwhile thing is
experience _levels_. The extra experience points a blessed gain level
gives you are only useful if you're low-level enough to make it feasible
to gain the rest by killing monsters. GL potions are rare enough that,
IME, you only identify them by the time that this is no longer feasible.
So, when you know what gain level is, it usually does not make any
difference whether you bless the potion or not; the next level is going
to have to come by magical means anyway.

